# 06 · Design System

**Status:** Locked 2026-05-11
**Implementation target:** `Z&Zplumbing-v2/components/` and `Z&Zplumbing-v2/tailwind.config.ts`

## Buttons

### Primary CTA (orange fill)

The default action button across the site. Used for Call buttons, Book Now, primary form submit, and any single most-important action on a page.

```
Background: hero-orange (#F96302)
Text: white
Border: none
Border radius: 0.375rem (6px)
Padding (lg): 1rem 1.75rem
Padding (md): 0.75rem 1.5rem
Font: Inter Bold, uppercase, 0.02em letter-spacing
Hover: brightness 0.95
Active: brightness 0.9, scale 0.98
```

### Secondary CTA (black fill)

For secondary actions like "Schedule Online" next to a primary Call CTA, or "Learn More" buttons.

```
Background: black
Text: white
Border: none
Border radius: 0.375rem
Hover: lighten to #1A1A1A
```

### Tertiary CTA (white with black border)

For low-priority actions like "View All Services" or breadcrumb-style navigation.

```
Background: white
Text: black
Border: 1.5px solid black
Border radius: 0.375rem
Hover: background light-gray
```

### Sizing tiers

| Size | Min height | Padding | Font size |
|---|---|---|---|
| sm | 32px | 0.5rem 1rem | 0.875rem (14px) |
| md | 40px | 0.75rem 1.5rem | 1rem (16px) |
| lg | 48px | 1rem 1.75rem | 1.125rem (18px) |
| xl | 56px | 1.25rem 2.25rem | 1.25rem (20px) |

Hero CTAs and sticky mobile CTAs use `lg` or `xl`. Form submit buttons use `md`. Inline body links that look like buttons use `sm`.

## Sticky mobile CTA bar

Fixed to the bottom of the viewport on mobile. Visible on every page except the booking widget overlay itself.

```
Position: fixed bottom-0 left-0 right-0
Height: 64px
Background: black
Inner padding: 0.5rem 1rem
Two buttons inside, side by side, flex:1 each:
  Left: Primary CTA (hero-orange fill, "CALL (510) 708-4237", phone icon)
  Right: Secondary CTA (white fill with black text, "Schedule", calendar icon)
Z-index: 50
Shadow above: 0 -4px 12px rgba(0,0,0,0.15)
```

Hidden on desktop (1024px+). Desktop has the same Call CTA inline in the sticky header.

## Sticky header

Fixed at the top of the viewport.

```
Height: 64px (mobile), 80px (desktop)
Background: white
Border-bottom: 1px solid light-gray
Inner padding: 0 1rem (mobile), 0 2rem (desktop)
Layout (mobile): logo left, phone icon button + mobile menu toggle right
Layout (desktop): logo left, main nav center, phone number + "Schedule" button right
Phone number on desktop: clickable tel: link, Barlow Condensed Bold, 1.25rem, in hero-orange
```

## Cards

### Service card

Used in service grids on the homepage and the services hub.

```
Background: white
Border: 1px solid light-gray
Border radius: 0.5rem (8px)
Padding: 1.5rem
Hover: border hero-orange, shadow 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.08), translateY(-2px)
Inner structure:
  Top: icon (24x24, hero-orange) OR small image (16:9, optional)
  Middle: H4 service name (Inter Bold)
  Body: 2 to 4 sentences description (Inter Regular, warm-gray)
  Footer: text link "Learn more →" (Inter SemiBold, hero-orange, no underline)
```

### Testimonial card

Used in the homepage testimonials carousel and the reviews page.

```
Background: light-gray
Border-radius: 0.5rem
Padding: 1.5rem
Inner structure:
  Top: 5-star row (orange filled stars, gray empty)
  Body: review text (Inter Regular, black, 1.0625rem)
  Footer: author first name + city + date (body-sm, warm-gray)
  Optional: small Google or Yelp icon
```

### Trust badge

Small badges used in trust strips, footer, hero subhead.

```
Background: transparent
Border: 1px solid light-gray
Border radius: 999px (pill)
Padding: 0.375rem 0.75rem
Font: body-xs uppercase tracked
Inner structure: optional small icon + label text
Examples:
  "CSLB #896116"
  "C-36 + A GENERAL ENGINEERING"
  "SINCE 2003"
  "24/7 EMERGENCY"
  "EBMUD COMPLIANT"
```

## Forms

### Input fields

```
Background: light-gray
Border: 1px solid transparent
Border radius: 0.375rem
Padding: 0.75rem 1rem
Min-height: 48px (touch target)
Font: Inter Regular, 1rem
Placeholder: warm-gray with 60% opacity
Focus: border hero-orange, background white, ring 2px hero-orange/20
Error: border danger-red, background white, ring 2px danger-red/15
Disabled: opacity 0.5, cursor not-allowed
```

### Labels

```
Font: Inter SemiBold, body-sm
Color: black
Margin-bottom: 0.25rem
Required indicator: red asterisk after label text
```

### Helper text

```
Font: Inter Regular, body-xs
Color: warm-gray
Margin-top: 0.25rem
```

### Error text

```
Font: Inter Medium, body-xs
Color: danger-red
Margin-top: 0.25rem
```

### Select / dropdown

Use shadcn `Select` primitive. Same input styling as text fields. Chevron icon in warm-gray on the right.

### Date / time picker

Use shadcn `Calendar` and `Popover` primitives. Selected date in hero-orange. Available time slots as button grid (sm size, white tertiary buttons).

## Sections

### Section padding

```
Vertical: 4rem top, 4rem bottom (mobile)
Vertical: 6rem top, 6rem bottom (desktop)
Horizontal: handled by the page container, not the section itself
```

### Section backgrounds

Alternate white and light-gray to create rhythm. Hero sections may use solid black with white text (rare, use sparingly to anchor a page).

### Container width

Max-width 1280px centered. Padding 1rem (mobile), 2rem (tablet+).

## Hero patterns

### Homepage hero

Full-width section. Black background OR a photo background with a black overlay at 60% opacity. Inside the container:
- Eyebrow label (hero-orange, uppercase, tracked)
- H1 (display-xl, white)
- Sub-headline (body-lg, white at 85% opacity)
- Zip-code search input + primary CTA button, inline
- Trust strip below: 4 to 5 trust badges in white outline

### Service / city page hero

Light-gray or white background. Inside the container:
- Eyebrow label (hero-orange)
- H1 (display-lg, black)
- Sub-headline (body-lg, warm-gray)
- Primary CTA (Call) + Secondary CTA (Schedule), inline
- Trust strip below

## Footer

```
Background: black
Text: white at 90% opacity for body, white for headers
Padding: 4rem top, 2rem bottom
Inner layout: 4-column grid on desktop, single column on mobile
Column 1: Logo (white variant) + tagline + phone CTA
Column 2: Services list
Column 3: Service areas list
Column 4: Company info (about, contact, blog, reviews, financing)
Bottom band: copyright, CSLB number, social icons (hero-orange on hover)
```

## Animation and motion

Minimal. The brand reads as confident, not flashy.

- Button hover: 150ms transition on background/border
- Card hover: 200ms transition on shadow + translateY
- Page transitions: native Next.js, no custom transitions in v1
- Scroll-triggered animations: avoid in v1. If a section needs entry animation, use a simple opacity-fade only.

## Spacing scale

Use Tailwind's default scale. Common values:
- `space-2` (8px) for tight grouping
- `space-4` (16px) for default element spacing
- `space-6` (24px) for related-but-distinct elements
- `space-12` (48px) for major content blocks
- `space-16` (64px) for section breathing room

## Iconography

Use `lucide-react` for system icons (Phone, Calendar, ChevronRight, MapPin, Check, X, Star, Clock). Hero-orange for accent icons, warm-gray for system icons.

Avoid custom illustrations in v1 except for the lateral diagram on the sewer-lateral-oakland page.

## Responsive breakpoints

Tailwind defaults:
- `sm`: 640px (large mobile / small tablet)
- `md`: 768px (tablet)
- `lg`: 1024px (small desktop)
- `xl`: 1280px (desktop)
- `2xl`: 1536px (large desktop)

Design for mobile first. Layouts add columns and increase scale at `md` and `lg`.

## Accessibility floor

- All interactive elements minimum 44x44px touch target
- Focus rings visible on every focusable element (hero-orange ring, 2px, with offset)
- Color is never the only indicator (icons + labels + state)
- Form labels always present, not placeholder-only
- Skip-to-main-content link on every page
- Semantic HTML: nav, main, article, section, footer where appropriate
- ARIA labels on icon-only buttons (sticky mobile Call button, etc.)
